@startuml
!include theme.puml
title Capacity evolution | Conceptual scaling, not deployed HA
top to bottom direction
rectangle "TARGET API replica group" #FFF5DE {
  component "Gateway / upstream balancing\nexplicit configuration required" as g
  component "Academic API replicas" as a
  component "Finance API replicas" as f
  component "HR API replicas" as h
  component "Identity API replicas\nshared key material + DB sessions" as i
}
database "Current shared PostgreSQL cluster\nfour service-owned databases\nconnection / CPU / I/O bottleneck" as db
queue "Current single RabbitMQ broker\nbroker availability bottleneck" as mq
rectangle "Worker scaling candidates" #FFF5DE {
  component "Outbox publisher replicas\nSKIP LOCKED batch selection" as w
  component "Finance consumers\nprefetch 10 + business idempotency" as c
}
g --> a
g --> f
g --> h
g --> i
a --> db
f --> db
h --> db
i --> db
w --> db
w --> mq
mq --> c
c --> db
note right of db
Measure before scaling:
 - p95 latency and request throughput
 - open DB connections / NullPool overhead
 - lock contention and report query plans
 - database storage and backup headroom
end note
note bottom of c
Replicas are NOT enabled by this diagram.
Review summary version races, payment polling scans,
refresh concurrency and rollout migration compatibility.
Single-host process replication does not provide host-failure HA.
end note
@enduml
